{
    "chapter_num": 12,
    "verses_count": 15,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Jephthah’s Conflict with Ephraim"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then the men of Ephraim "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "were summoned"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "gathered together, crossed over toward Zaphon, and said to Jephthah, “Why did you cross over to fight against the people of Ammon, and did not call us to go with you? We will burn your house down on you with fire!”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Jephthah said to them, “My people and I were in a great struggle with the people of Ammon; and when I called you, you did not deliver me out of their hands. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So when I saw that you would not deliver "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "me,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " I took my life in my hands and crossed over against the people of Ammon; and the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " delivered them into my hand. Why then have you come up to me this day to fight against me?” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now Jephthah gathered together all the men of Gilead and fought against Ephraim. And the men of Gilead defeated Ephraim, because they said, “You Gileadites "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "are"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " fugitives of Ephraim among the Ephraimites "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "and"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " among the Manassites.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "The Gileadites seized the fords of the Jordan before the Ephraimites "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "arrived."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " And when "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "any"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Ephraimite who escaped said, “Let me cross over,” the men of Gilead would say to him, “"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "Are"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " you an Ephraimite?” If he said, “No,” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "then they would say to him, “Then say, ‘Shibboleth’!”"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. a flowing stream; used as a test of dialect"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " And he would say, “Sibboleth,” for he could not "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. speak so"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "pronounce "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "it"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " right. Then they would take him and kill him at the fords of the Jordan. There fell at that time forty-two thousand Ephraimites."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Jephthah judged Israel six years. Then Jephthah the Gileadite died and was buried among the cities of Gilead."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Ibzan, Elon, and Abdon"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "After him, Ibzan of Bethlehem judged Israel. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "He had thirty sons. And he gave away thirty daughters in marriage, and brought in thirty daughters from elsewhere for his sons. He judged Israel seven years. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Ibzan died and was buried at Bethlehem."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "After him, Elon the Zebulunite judged Israel. He judged Israel ten years. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Elon the Zebulunite died and was buried at Aijalon in the country of Zebulun."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "After him, Abdon the son of Hillel the Pirathonite judged Israel. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "He had forty sons and thirty grandsons, who rode on seventy young donkeys. He judged Israel eight years. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Abdon the son of Hillel the Pirathonite died and was buried in Pirathon in the land of Ephraim, in the mountains of the Amalekites."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}